<%- /*
The trigger, the draft step and every later step's condition are the hosted gate shape
(templates/hostedgate.go, defined in internal/ghworkflow/hostedgate.go): the job runs on a push to
the default branch and on every pull request activity that can change what merges, and on a draft
it fails in its first step, saying it runs when the pull request is marked ready (#817). Every
rendering this body or an earlier one produced is recorded (internal/flavor/ci_prior.go), so an
unedited copy is refreshed without --force.
*/ -%>
---
name: CI

<% hostedGateOn %>
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-26.04
    # Every cargo step builds with rustc warnings as errors (HISS-10), the test
    # build included; praetorctl audit fails a cargo lane without it.
    env:
      RUSTFLAGS: -D warnings
    steps:
<% hostedGateDraftStep %>
      - name: Checkout source<% hostedGateStepIf %>
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      # rustup ships on the hosted runner image, so the toolchain needs no
      # third-party action.
      - name: Install the stable toolchain<% hostedGateStepIf %>
        run: |
          rustup toolchain install stable --profile minimal \
            --component clippy,rustfmt
          rustup default stable

      - name: Check formatting<% hostedGateStepIf %>
        run: cargo fmt --all -- --check

      - name: Lint<% hostedGateStepIf %>
        run: cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings

      - name: Test<% hostedGateStepIf %>
        run: cargo test --all-features
